    "title": "Fredericksburg is ready to 'Rumble' on Saturday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kathy Knotts ,\n8 hours ago If you’ve ever heard a raw, distorted guitar riff blast out of a movie trailer and felt your pulse kick up a notch, you’ve heard a bit of Fredericksburg. That sound — the one so menacing some radio stations banned it in 1958 — was born by accident at a sock hop at the old Fredericksburg Armory, when a local guitarist named Link Wray couldn’t remember the chords to a song he’d been asked to play and improvised something else entirely. Read full article\n1",
